VI. Extraction Guidelines
- Experimental information may be scattered across multiple chunks. Combine fields from different chunks only when they clearly describe the same Experiment_id.
- Each record must have more than one extractable field. If no experimental conditions can be extracted, do not output it. If an extraction field has multiple reported values (e.g., pH 3/5/7/10; Fe^2+ 1/2/3/5 mM; time 10/60 min), record all levels as a comma-separated <measurement> list within a single value (e.g., Fe^2+_1,2,3,5_mM). 
- Evaluate evidence separately for each record and assign a condition only when the text unambiguously scopes it to that record (or its named trial group). Carryover of component is allowed only when the text explicitly makes it clear that the same component applies to both scenarios.
- If a field is not supported by evidence in the provided source chunks or figure caption, omit that field line entirely—do not output null, blanks/placeholders, or inferred values. 
- Apply the following standardization rules for each component when applicable.
